      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "SAM2Matting — tensor alpha workflow\n\nUse this advanced workflow only when the propagated alpha must feed ComfyUI IMAGE/MASK nodes. For normal background replacement and matte-video export, use sam2matting_video_default.json instead.\n\n1. Upload a video and a black/white seed-mask image. White = foreground.\n2. The seed mask must match the video frame selected by mask_frame (zero-based).\n3. The loader and both encoders are set to 24 fps. Change all three together if needed.\n4. frame_load_cap is 48 for a quick first test; use 0 to process the complete clip.\n\nOutputs: transparent VP9 WebM and a black-background/white-foreground H.264 matte video. The matting node returns only alpha; the original video feeds Join Image with Alpha directly to avoid caching duplicate RGB and preview batches. Invert Mask converts white-foreground opacity to ComfyUI's inverse-mask convention."
      ],
      "color": "#243447",
      "bgcolor": "#34506b"
    },
